This file exists so the scheduled keep-alive workflow can record repository
activity roughly once a month.

GitHub automatically disables scheduled workflows in a repository that has seen
no activity for 60 days. Because attendance here is recorded monthly, the repo
can easily go quiet for longer than that — at which point the keep-alive would
stop running and the Supabase project would be paused, then eventually deleted.

The workflow updates this file only when the most recent commit is more than 30
days old, so it adds about a dozen commits a year and nothing more.
